 p=ROOT/'POST REVIEW.txt';p.write_text(p.read_text()+'\nORIGINAL TASK SCHEDULER / YIELD — '+now+'\n'+game+'\nWHO DID WHAT: Codex coordinator inspected original vector0x80->0xde08 and complete handler/wrapper bytes, consulted NXP M68000PRM TRAP printed4-188 andRTE printed6-84, then authored callback C with an explicit CPU continuation state. C preserves11callee-saved register push/pop order, six-byte exception frame, linked-context skip/read logic, unsigned timer comparison/rereads, selected PC/SR/USP and fresh-task transfers. Output CPU state is committed only on success; prior memory writes remain on host failures.\nUnicorn capability probe executed the original handler through0xde5a but failed atRTE withUC_ERR_EXCEPTION. Its ISP accessor returnedzero in that probe. No RTE patch was accepted as native control-flow proof. A second capability probe used existing pinned core exports and originalRTE successfully restored the selectedPC/userstack. No core changes were made.\nThe checker invokes the pinned nativeCPU one instruction at a time, supplying fixed RAM/context fixtures, no GPU/DSP/game frames or external interrupts. Read-only D/A/USP/ISP prefix matches pinnedcpudefs.h; register setup uses existingCPU APIs. Declared changing timer/clock reads are injected just before their original load instructions; native CPU executes branches,TRAP,RTE,MOVEM,RTS and stores. WholeRAM and allregisters/PC/SR/stackbanks match C. A separate originalUnicorn prefix supplies exact bus widths/values/order up toRTE; finaltwoRTEreads follow the documented frame and nativeCPU implementation, not claimed as Unicorn execution.\n32-case preflight and initial512-case run passed. Coordinator then found the fixture task count and scenario both depended on the same variant modulo: the high-bit deadline scenario always had one task and never exercised that value. The task-count formula was decoupled, high-bit/unsigned clock pairs expanded, and the full512-case run repeated. Latest run passes312different-context cases,20fresh entries,28actualhigh-bit deadline reads; all26instructions and18hostguards. The earlier run/report is retained. Canonical C required no changes.\nLatest exact fixtures/native PCs/CPU states/C bus traces:\n'+str(Path(checks['directory'])/'fixtures.json')+'\nVerifier report:\n'+str(ROOT/evidence[0])+'\n'+quality+'\n'+frontend+'\nInitial ordinary prompts/responses, including rejected contradiction:\n'+str(initial_path.parent/'prompts-and-responses.txt')+'\nExact-question retry:\n'+str(path.parent/'prompts-and-responses.txt')+'\nCoordinator review:\n'+str(ROOT/evidence[4])+'\nPrimary architecture reference:\nhttps://www.nxp.com/docs/en/reference-manual/M68000PRM.pdf\n\n'+pending+'\n')
